Ruby() User's guide

Ruby() is a life simulation game, the goal of this game is to plan the main character's life event to achieve different endings.


For the text on the game, simply click on the screen to read the text.
The simulation part takes 36 tracks, click the event you want to choose, then click continue button to move forward.
After the 36th track, the game will automatically calculate your score, and display the final ending.


Enjoy your time with Ruby()!

